# VTID-03771 — commands run during investigation and verification

## Investigation (read-only, live oasis_events tracing)

User reported the exact VTID-03763/03770-shaped symptom recurring live on
staging, right after VTID-03770 shipped and was confirmed deployed. Queried
live `oasis_events` (Supabase MCP, read-only SELECT) for a real tap made
during this session, topic T005, real account bc34a5ca-6966-44f6-9507-
3bed98e3e1d5:

  - Confirmed the guided-topic candidate won the wake-brief ranker
    (dedupe_key:"guided_topic:T005", winner:true) — the tap itself worked.
  - Confirmed a `nova_validation` content-filter block on the FIRST
    attempt, still turn_count:0.
  - Confirmed the SAME session's internal retry
    (nova_premature_close_retry -> greeting_recovery) fired next — this is
    resendGreetingIfStuckAtZeroTurns, NOT a client-side reconnect (ruled
    out VTID-03746/VTID-03770's code paths as the cause — those are
    client-triggered new-session-start functions; this defect is a
    same-session, server-internal retry).
  - Critically found `stage=newday_briefing_eval` then
    `stage=stamp_briefing_date_write` inside THIS retry's diag trace —
    stages that only exist inside the "safe fast greeting" branch's
    new-day-overview evaluation, never inside guided-topic delivery. This
    is what confirmed the retry substituted a daily briefing for the
    guided topic, rather than losing/dropping the topic silently.
  - Confirmed via a second, later live tap (same session continuing) that
    audio_out grew to 394 chunks on a single turn (the daily-briefing
    content, not T005) and then the session idled indefinitely — turn_count
    stuck at 1, audio_out never advancing again despite 2+ minutes of
    continuous vtid.live.audio.in.chunk events from the user.

Traced the code path via grep + Read:
  grep -n "resendGreetingIfStuckAtZeroTurns\|nova_premature_close_retry\|greeting_recovery" src/routes/orb-live.ts
  grep -n "function sendGreetingPromptToLiveAPI\|decideOpening(" src/routes/orb-live.ts
  grep -n "newday_briefing_eval\|stamp_briefing_date_write\|guided_topic_id" src/routes/orb-live.ts

Read `sendGreetingPromptToLiveAPI` (orb-live.ts:9714 onward) end-to-end.
Confirmed via a brace-matching awk script that the safe-fast `if` block
(starting at the `contextReadyResolved === false` condition) spans through
a `return true;` statement BEFORE the normal ladder's `_hasPendingGuided-
TopicAtOpen` computation and `decideOpening()` call — i.e. once the
safe-fast branch's condition is met, the function returns without ever
reaching the guided-topic protection that already exists further down
(VTID-03727):

  awk 'NR==9755{depth=0} NR>=9755{for(i=1;i<=length($0);i++){c=substr($0,i,1); \
    if(c=="{")depth++; if(c=="}"){depth--; if(depth==0 && NR>9755){print NR; exit}}}}' \
    src/routes/orb-live.ts

## Implementation

Edits to `services/gateway/src/routes/orb-live.ts`:
  - Hoisted `const _hasPendingGuidedTopicAtOpen = !!(session as
    any).guidedTopicNarrationContent && (session.turn_count || 0) === 0;`
    from its original site (just before the normal ladder's
    `decideOpening()` call) to immediately before the safe-fast branch's
    `if` statement.
  - Added `&& !_hasPendingGuidedTopicAtOpen` to the safe-fast branch's `if`
    condition (previously only `contextReadyResolved === false &&
    !session.isAnonymous`).
  - Removed the now-duplicate declaration at the original site, replacing
    it with a one-line comment noting the flag is reused from the hoisted
    declaration above (a literal duplicate `const` in the same function
    scope would not compile).

